    "role": "COMPOSITION_DIRECTION_ONLY",
    "reason": "The forest-bounded clearing restores unfinished landscape, packed post feet replace fantasy sockets, and posts, uninstalled hearth matter, storage and roofing fibre remain physically reachable in one continuous portrait world. The inherited former footprint is still too quiet at phone scale, so production inputs remain blocked."
  },
  "mandatoryRefinements": [
    "Make one complete offset former footprint and its reworn threshold readable at 390-point width without outlines, glow, grids or open-hole confusion.",
    "Separate old filled post marks, current open postholes and packed accepted posts through material state rather than colour coding.",
    "Replace the oversized foreground shaft with progressive wedges, tamped loess and soil displacement around the accepted post.",
    "Author bare, posts, hearth-first, storage-first, hearth-and-storage, roof-available and roof-settled states as separable assets.",
    "Keep the first clearing bounded by substantial woodland so later settlement expansion remains visible work.",
    "Give every manipulated component and destination a minimum 44-point effective touch envelope at the smallest supported crop.",
    "Prove the load path from packed post through frame to roof without modern truss geometry or interface light."
  ],
